              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Mandarin for to thunder, then the Mandarin for pleasantly cool."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: 节日",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "节日 — jiérì — \"festival\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "今天是什么节日 jīntiān shì shénme jiérì — What festival is it today?"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The new character, in pieces: 节 (jié) — the grass piece on top, a bar crossed by two short verticals, and under it a bar that turns down into a hook, with a long vertical through it. The next lesson puts it in your hand."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "节日 (jiérì) is built from 节 (jié) 'a joint' and 日 'day', both inherited from Middle Chinese, tset and nyit (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription); the dictionary quotes an older book for the first: the joint of a bamboo. A festival as a joint in the year is the likely image, though it is not given there."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for times of day."
            }
          ]
        },
